why Defensive Stance at 10 and a one-hand weapon of your choice from Stormwind, Ironforge or Darnassus.

# The Alliance Defensive Stance quests at level 10, every race in one guide:
# - Human: A Warrior's Training (1638) from Lyria Du Lac in Goldshire or Ilsa
#   Corbin in Stormwind, Bartleby the Drunk, Beat Bartleby, Bartleby's Mug
#   (1639, 1640, 1665: Defensive Stance), Marshal Haggard and Dead-tooth Jack
#   (1666, 1667: Haggard's Axe, Hammer, Dagger or Sword).
# - Dwarf and Gnome: Muren Stormpike (1679) from Granis Swiftaxe in Kharanos,
#   Vejrek (1678: Defensive Stance), Tormus Deepforge, Ironband's Compound and
#   Grey Iron Weapons (1680-1682: Umbral Axe, Mace, Dagger or Sword).
# - Night Elf: Elanaria (1684) from Moon Priestess Amara or Kyra Windblade at
#   Dolanaar, Vorlus Vilehoof (1683: Defensive Stance), The Shade of Elura,
#   Smith Mathiel and Weapons of Elunite (1686, 1692, 1693: Elunite Axe,
#   Hammer, Dagger or Sword).
# - Skyborne: The Skybreaker Bulwark (94003, Forever-new) from Seena
#   Skybreaker in Valanaar on Zephras Isle (Defensive Stance and the
#   Stormforged Protector shield); Forever's quest data also opens the city
#   roads to them, so Bartleby's road is offered for a weapon afterwards.
# The three city roads exclude each other (TDB exclusive groups: A Warrior's
# Training, Muren Stormpike and Elanaria; Bartleby the Drunk, Vejrek and
# Vorlus Vilehoof): any Alliance warrior may take any one. Holding one blocks
# the others (Harry or Bartleby will not talk to you): abandon it first. The
# guide offers each race its home road first and the Stormwind road last; its
# steps after the first accept carry no race filter but `when !turnedin 1679`
# and `when !turnedin 1684`, so a Dwarf, Gnome or Night Elf who took A
# Warrior's Training from Ilsa Corbin is led through it (their home steps pass
# once those quests are closed to them). Lint warns that 1639 is
# closed after the home roads earlier in the chain: it reads the chain straight
# through and does not apply those `when` lines.
# Sources: quests.json, npcs.json, objects.json and items.json for the
# chains, givers, mobs, key, chests and crates; quest-notes for levels,
# respawns, the hidden trails and huts, the wreck and the guards; Forever's
# Warrior class quest list (data/local/quest-audit/): Bartleby's Mug, Vejrek
# and Vorlus Vilehoof now teach Defensive Stance; the weapon choices are
# unchanged; The Skybreaker Bulwark is new. The leveling routes do the
# Defensive Stance part on the way; this guide is for anyone off the route
# and adds each race's weapon.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Skyborne: The Skybreaker Bulwark

step Seena Skybreaker in Valanaar
  only Skyborne
  zone Zephras Isle
  tip At 10, Seena Skybreaker stands with the trainers by Valanaar's west gate. A cultist, Zaal Stormshield, holds her family's shield at the Shrine of Akir.
  level 10
  accept 94003                                -- Seena Skybreaker

step Zaal Stormshield
  only Skyborne
  tip Head north-west from Valanaar to the Shrine of Akir. Zaal Stormshield stands west of the shrine's approach, among the cult's Guardians, Spiritcallers and Blademasters: pull them one at a time before you take him. He drops the Skybreaker Bulwark.
  kill 257196                                 -- Zaal Stormshield
  collect 263993 quest 94003.1                -- Skybreaker Bulwark, from Zaal Stormshield

step The Skybreaker Bulwark
  only Skyborne
  tip Back to Seena in Valanaar. She teaches Defensive Stance and gives you the Stormforged Protector, a shield to use it with. Bartleby's road below still gives a weapon, once you reach Stormwind.
  turnin 94003 reward 275290                  -- Seena Skybreaker: Defensive Stance

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Dwarf and Gnome: Vejrek and Tormus Deepforge

step Muren Stormpike
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip At 10, Granis Swiftaxe, the warrior trainer in Kharanos, sends you to Muren Stormpike in Ironforge. Any Alliance warrior may take one of the three roads, never two: in Stormwind at 10 anyway? Ilsa Corbin's A Warrior's Training is the quickest stance (one fight in a tavern), with a Haggard's weapon after it.
  level 10
  accept 1679                                 -- Granis Swiftaxe

step Muren Stormpike in Ironforge
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Ironforge
  tip Muren Stormpike stands in the Hall of Arms in the Military Ward.
  turnin 1679                                 -- Muren Stormpike
  accept 1678

step Vejrek
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Vejrek (level 11, a lone troll) waits at his hut on a hill south of Frostmane Hold, near the mountains at the top of a short ramp, with no other trolls around; the hut at the front of Frostmane Hold is the wrong one. He fights in Defensive Stance and sunders your armor; Thunder Clap slows him. His head always drops; he returns about 8 minutes after dying.
  collect 6799 quest 1678.1                   -- Vejrek's Head

step Tormus Deepforge
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Ironforge
  tip Back to Muren for Defensive Stance, then to Tormus Deepforge at the Great Forge in the middle of Ironforge.
  turnin 1678                                 -- Muren Stormpike: Defensive Stance
  accept 1680
  turnin 1680                                 -- Tormus Deepforge
  accept 1681

step Ironband's Compound
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Dun Morogh
  tip Ironband's Compound lies in eastern Dun Morogh, below Helm's Bed Lake on its south side. Dark Iron Spies (level 8-10) stand along the way, far enough apart to pull one at a time. Ironband's Strongbox is in the basement of the southernmost house; Captain Beld (level 11) stands by it and charges on sight. The box always holds the ore and refills 15 minutes after opening.
  collect 6800 quest 1681.1                   -- Umbral Ore, from Ironband's Strongbox

step Grey Iron Weapons
  only Dwarf,Gnome
  zone Ironforge
  turnin 1681                                 -- Tormus Deepforge
  accept 1682
  turnin 1682 choose 6978 6982 6981 6984      -- Tormus Deepforge

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Night Elf: Vorlus and the Shade of Elura

step Elanaria
  only NightElf
  zone Teldrassil
  tip At 10, Kyra Windblade, the warrior trainer in Dolanaar, or Moon Priestess Amara, who patrols the road west of Dolanaar, sends you to Elanaria on the Warrior's Terrace in Darnassus. Any Alliance warrior may take one of the three roads, never two: in Stormwind at 10 anyway? Ilsa Corbin's A Warrior's Training teaches the same stance after one fight in a tavern.
  level 10
  accept 1684 npc 3598                        -- Kyra Windblade

step Elanaria in Darnassus
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip Elanaria stands on the Warrior's Terrace.
  turnin 1684                                 -- Elanaria
  accept 1683

step Vorlus Vilehoof
  only NightElf
  zone Teldrassil
  tip Vorlus Vilehoof (level 10, a satyr) stands at a hidden moonwell up a hillside west of Dolanaar. The trail is hard to spot: it starts behind a Gnarlpine camp and climbs in switchbacks lined with lamp posts. The furbolgs below can come in groups. His horn always drops; he returns 5 minutes after dying.
  collect 6805 quest 1683.1                   -- Horn of Vorlus

step The Shade of Elura
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  turnin 1683                                 -- Elanaria: Defensive Stance
  accept 1686

step Elunite under Auberdine
  only NightElf
  zone Darkshore
  tip Take the boat from Rut'theran Village to Auberdine. The wreck lies underwater just south of Auberdine's southern pier, where the Menethil boat docks. Open Crates of Elunite on the sea floor around the wreck, by a huge sunken turtle, toward the beach and under the pier until you have eight; every crate holds ore and comes back in 3-5 minutes. The grey Shade of Elura (level 11) drifts around the middle of the wreck and always drops the medallion: target it when you see it, so you can find it after surfacing for air. Watch your breath; Threshers can join in.
  collect 6808 x8 quest 1686.1                -- Elunite Ore, from Crates of Elunite
  collect 6809 quest 1686.2                   -- Elura's Medallion, from the Shade of Elura

step Smith Mathiel
  only NightElf
  zone Darnassus
  tip Back on the Warrior's Terrace: Elanaria hands you the Case of Elunite; Mathiel works on the far, south side of the same terrace, easy to miss.
  turnin 1686                                 -- Elanaria
  accept 1692
  turnin 1692                                 -- Mathiel
  accept 1693
  turnin 1693 choose 6966 6968 6969 6967      -- Mathiel

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Stormwind (Human, Skyborne, or anyone who took this road): Bartleby and Marshal Haggard

step A Warrior's Training
  only Human,Skyborne
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip At 10, Lyria Du Lac, the warrior trainer by the inn in Goldshire, sends you to Harry Burlguard in Stormwind; Ilsa Corbin, the warrior trainer in Stormwind's Old Town, offers it too.
  level 10
  accept 1638 npc 913                         -- Lyria Du Lac

step Bartleby
  when !turnedin 1679
  when !turnedin 1684
  zone Stormwind City
  tip Harry Burlguard and Bartleby are in the Pig and Whistle tavern in Old Town; Bartleby is the drunk at the far end of the bar. Bartleby (level 10) hits harder than his level, so start at full health; he gives up at low health instead of dying. If he wins, he disappears for about three minutes: keep the quest and talk to him again when he is back. A Dwarf, Gnome or Night Elf who took A Warrior's Training from Ilsa Corbin instead of their home road is led through Stormwind from here.
  turnin 1638                                 -- Harry Burlguard
  accept 1639
  turnin 1639                                 -- Bartleby
  accept 1640
  kill 6090 quest 1640.1                      -- Beat Bartleby
  turnin 1640                                 -- Bartleby
  accept 1665
  turnin 1665                                 -- Harry Burlguard: Defensive Stance
  accept 1666

step Marshal Haggard
  when !turnedin 1679
  when !turnedin 1684
  zone Elwynn Forest
  tip Marshal Haggard's manor stands at the south-east edge of the Eastvale Logging Camp in eastern Elwynn, at the end of a short road that does not join the main one.
  turnin 1666                                 -- Marshal Haggard
  accept 1667

step Dead-tooth Jack
  when !turnedin 1679
  when !turnedin 1684
  tip Dead-Tooth Jack (level 11) camps in the far south-east of Elwynn. A guard stands beside him and Defias and wolves are spread around the camp (now and then a rarer guard too): clear them one at a time, then kill Jack. He always drops Dead-tooth's Key; open Dead-tooth's Strongbox in the crates by him for Marshal Haggard's Badge. Jack returns 3 minutes after dying, the box 1 minute after opening.
  collect 6783 "Dead-tooth's Key"             -- from Dead-Tooth Jack
  collect 6782 quest 1667.1                   -- Marshal Haggard's Badge, from Dead-tooth's Strongbox

step Back to Marshal Haggard
  when !turnedin 1679
  when !turnedin 1684
  turnin 1667 choose 6979 6983 6980 6985      -- Marshal Haggard
